@startuml sd_cqrs_route_events
title Scenario (Assignment 2): a route created on one replica reaches the read model of every replica

autonumber
actor "ATCC" as c
participant "airports-routes-1\n(write side)" as r1
database "DB replica 1\nroute, replica_state" as db1
participant "airports-routes-2\n(next in the ring)" as r2
queue "RabbitMQ\nexchange airports-routes.events\n(topic)" as mq
participant "airports-routes-0, -1, -2\n(read side)" as listeners
database "DB of each replica\nroute_view" as views

c -> r1 : POST /api/routes {OPO-CDG} (JWT)
r1 -> db1 : save route + stamp of the change\n(one transaction)
r1 -> r2 : copy of the route (replication, as in Assignment 1)
r1 -> mq : after the commit: route.created\n{key, status, version, data, stamp}
r1 --> c : 201
note over mq
  One durable queue per replica
  (airports-routes.read-model.<replica>),
  bound with route.*: every replica gets
  every route event (publish/subscribe)
end note
mq -> listeners : route.created (to each queue)
listeners -> views : RouteEventListener: apply if later than the stamp kept\n(last writer wins, as the replication)

== read side ==
c -> listeners : GET /api/routes/search (any replica)
listeners -> views : read route_view (local, no peers asked)
listeners --> c : 200, every route of every replica

== a lost event (broker down when it was published) ==
listeners -> listeners : RouteViewReconciler, on startup and every 60 s:\nwhat this replica and its peers hold (GET /internal/replicas/routes)
listeners -> views : apply the changes later than the ones kept
@enduml
